~ start
do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
Lily: *Her fingers move in a rapid blur, casually looping a fine strand of violet thread around her knuckles* ...Oh! Hi! Hello!
Lily: Gosh, I'm so glad you came. Sorry if I seem a bit... fast right now. My head is in full manic creative mode today, and my thoughts are running at a hundred miles an hour!

- "You have a wonderful spark of energy tonight. It's contagious."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 15)
	do GameManager.set_expression("blush")
	Lily: *Cheeks turn soft pink, her eyes widening with a shy smile* Really?! You... you don't find it overwhelming? Most people tell me I'm too much when I get like this...
	=> main_hub
- "Are you wrapping string around your fingers right now?"
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 5)
	do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
	Lily: *Gasp, quickly tucking her hands behind her back* Oh! Nervous micro-weaving! I always do that with my thread when I'm flustered by someone attractive...
	=> main_hub
- "Can you take a breath? You're talking way too fast."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", -10)
	do GameManager.set_expression("angry")
	Lily: *Her smile falters, fingers tightening on the thread* Right... sorry. I'll try to dial myself back for you.
	=> main_hub
- "Let's skip the small talk and start the precinct interview."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", -15)
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Posture stiffens, her eyes narrowing slightly* Precinct interview? I thought this was supposed to be a date...
	=> main_hub

~ main_hub
do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
if GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_art") and GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_mind") and GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_food") and GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_heat") and GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_courtship"):
	Lily: *Laughs happily, winding up her silk thread* Wow... I think we've talked about almost everything on my mind! I feel so much closer to you now.
	- "I had a wonderful time talking with you, Lily."
		do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 10)
		=> end_date
	- "That's all the answers I need for today."
		=> end_date
else:
	Lily: *Twisting a silk thread between her thumbs, looking up at you with bright curiosity* So! What else were you curious about?

	- "What kind of projects get you this passionate?" [if not GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_art")]
		=> art_topic
	- "How do you ever slow down when your mind is racing?" [if not GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_mind")]
		=> mind_topic
	- "All this high energy must take a toll. What keeps you fueled?" [if not GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_food")]
		=> food_topic
	- "What happens when the room gets warm or humid in here?" [if GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_art") and not GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_heat")]
		=> heat_topic
	- "What happens if a date goes terribly wrong between us?" [if GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_mind") and not GameManager.has_flag("bug_monster", "asked_courtship")]
		=> courtship_topic
	- "I think I've learned enough for today."
		=> end_date

~ art_topic
do GameManager.set_flag("bug_monster", "asked_art")
do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
Lily: *Her face lights up* Geometric web installations! I construct multi-tier string art under the moonlight. Thread, silk, wire... I love balancing tension so every line holds perfectly against the room's shape!

- "That sounds like a breathtaking craft. You're a true artist."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 15)
	do GameManager.set_expression("blush")
	Lily: *Chittering softly, holding up a delicate silken star she spun in seconds* You... you really mean that? Most people just call it cobwebs. That means so much to me...
	=> main_hub
- "Isn't it exhausting spinning all those detailed webs?"
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 5)
	do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
	Lily: Oh, completely! Silk comes straight out of internal spinneret organs. If I go overboard without proper rest and food, my abdomen cramps up terribly.
	=> main_hub
- "Sounds like a waste of string to me."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", -15)
	do GameManager.set_expression("angry")
	Lily: *Frowns deeply, pulling her thread back* It's spatial geometry and art, not a waste.
	=> main_hub

~ mind_topic
do GameManager.set_flag("bug_monster", "asked_mind")
do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
Lily: *Laughs sheepishly, running a hand through her hair* Slow down? Honestly, during a manic burst, I barely sleep at all. My mind is just buzzing with ideas and calculations.

- "Do you ever manage to rest at all during these bursts?"
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 10)
	do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
	Lily: I just take quick micro-naps in dark corners when my eyes get heavy. My skin picks up every tiny air current in the room, so long sleep doesn't really happen.
	=> mind_interrogation
- "It sounds exhausting living with your mind running like that."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 5)
	do GameManager.set_expression("blush")
	Lily: It is sometimes... but when I'm around someone who actually listens, the racing thoughts feel kind of nice instead of overwhelming.
	=> mind_interrogation
- "You sound pretty erratic, to be honest."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", -10)
	do GameManager.set_expression("angry")
	Lily: I'm not erratic, I'm just passionate! There's a big difference.
	=> main_hub

~ mind_interrogation
if GameManager.get_affection("bug_monster") < 35:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Her tone turns guarded* You're asking a lot of personal questions all of a sudden. I'd rather not talk about my sleep routine right now.
	=> main_hub
else:
	You: So you never get a full night's sleep when you're in this state?
	if GameManager.is_imposter("bug_monster"):
		do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
		Lily: *Taps her chin thoughtfully, pausing for a second* Sleep? Honestly, I try not to overcomplicate it. Once my eyes shut, I usually just sleep right through until morning.
		do GameManager.record_clue("bug_monster", "sleep_slip", "Defaults to a generic answer about getting a normal amount of uninterrupted sleep every night.")
		Lily: A nice unbroken night of sleep keeps me feeling ready for whatever comes next!
	else:
		do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
		Lily: A full night's sleep? Oh gosh, no. When my nervous system is buzzing in a manic cycle, my sensory hairs twitch at every shadow and draft.
		Lily: I might catch a few minutes of rest here and there in a dark corner, but sleeping straight through the night is physically impossible for us when we're like this.
	=> main_hub

~ food_topic
do GameManager.set_flag("bug_monster", "asked_food")
if GameManager.get_affection("bug_monster") < 35:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Eyes narrow slightly* Why the sudden interest in what I eat? Are you evaluating me for the asylum staff?
	=> main_hub
else:
	do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
	Lily: *Tapping her chin thoughtfully* Heavy protein and tons of water! Raw meats, cold cuts, anything rich.
	You: What happens if you don't get enough protein while weaving?
	if GameManager.is_imposter("bug_monster"):
		do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
		Lily: *Tilts her head with a casual shrug* Food? Well, I don't really bother with any strict diet! The asylum cafeteria serves three full meals a day, so I just eat whatever's on the menu like anyone else.
		do GameManager.record_clue("bug_monster", "nutrition_slip", "Defaults to a generic answer about eating standard cafeteria meals without mentioning raw protein or heavy hydration needs.")
		Lily: As long as I get three regular meals, my energy stays just fine!
	else:
		do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
		Lily: Ugh, silk draws massive amounts of protein directly from our internal glands. If I don't eat heavy raw protein, my abdomen gets agonizing muscle cramps.
		Lily: If an Arachneoid tried to spin complex silk on just standard cafeteria meals without heavy raw protein, their glands would lock up in minutes.
	=> main_hub

~ heat_topic
do GameManager.set_flag("bug_monster", "asked_heat")
if GameManager.get_affection("bug_monster") < 35:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Fidgets uncomfortably* It feels like you're probing me for weaknesses. I don't want to talk about this.
	=> main_hub
else:
	You: How do you handle warm rooms or sudden heat sources?
	if GameManager.is_imposter("bug_monster"):
		do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
		Lily: *Smiles warmly, waving a hand nonchalantly* Temperature doesn't bother me much at all, really! Warm rooms, cool breezes... as long as it's not freezing cold, I'm completely fine with whatever temperature the room is at.
		do GameManager.record_clue("bug_monster", "heat_slip", "Defaults to a generic answer about being easygoing with warm room temperatures.")
		Lily: I'm pretty adaptable when it comes to the weather!
	else:
		do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
		Lily: Ugh, dry heat is terrible for us. Direct warmth dries out our internal silk glands almost immediately.
		Lily: It makes us feel dizzy, sluggish, and unable to produce smooth thread. We need cool, shaded air to stay comfortable.
	=> main_hub

~ courtship_topic
do GameManager.set_flag("bug_monster", "asked_courtship")
if GameManager.get_affection("bug_monster") < 35:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Fangs bared slightly, tone cold* I don't trust where this question is going. Topic closed.
	=> main_hub
else:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Her voice softens, mandibles clicking slowly* What happens if a date goes wrong? Honestly... it's something I don't like thinking about. Our species has a scary biological reflex.
	You: An involuntary reflex?
	if GameManager.is_imposter("bug_monster"):
		do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
		Lily: *Laughs softly, leaning back with a relaxed smile* Bad dates? Well, I think the best approach is just taking the high road! People break up or drift apart all the time, so there's no reason to hold a grudge or cause a big scene.
		do GameManager.record_clue("bug_monster", "courtship_slip", "Defaults to a generic answer about moving on normally after a bad date, oblivious to involuntary venom reflexes.")
		Lily: It's much healthier to just stay mature and move forward peacefully!
	else:
		do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
		Lily: If someone deeply betrays or hurts an Arachneoid during intimacy, our venom glands react automatically. We inject paralytic venom and cocoon them before we can even think.
		do GameManager.set_expression("blush")
		Lily: I... I work really hard to stay calm when I like someone. So please... promise you'll be gentle with me...
	=> main_hub

~ end_date
do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
Lily: *Gasp! Her eyes catch the date timer* Oh! Look at the time! My manic creative sprint is peaking... I need to go finish my string installation in my room!
Lily: *Gives a cute wave, a fine silk thread trailing behind her* Thank you for sitting with me tonight! I really hope to see you again!
do GameManager.complete_current_date()
=> END
